    req_app_io_001_regex_sffi_migration_missing_2026-09-18, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-20261127: state at tip - the doc's pinning spec legacy_ffi_facades_spec was already green (regex_ffi rerouted earlier + owner module built), but the public regex surface was still raw/unsafe (every re-exported fn @unsafe - callers needed unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]) blocks - and the app facade re-exported raw rt_regex_* ABI names; regex_sffi_spec was a skipped placeholder). Fix (3 files, pure-Simple): src/app/io/regex_sffi.spl rewritten from raw re-export into the canonical safe facade (safe wrappers with identical signatures/docstrings/semantics incl regex_new_checked/regex_is_match_checked/regex_is_match_quick_checked forwarding to the owner via aliased imports; helpers/validators reimplemented identically; explicit export block per the sqlite_sffi idiom; no raw externs, no rt_*, no @unsafe on the public surface); src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/io/regex_sffi.spl gained the explicit export block for the safe surface (owner keeps handle/ABI policy and its confined @unsafe wrappers per the compress/ftp idiom); test/01_unit/app/io/regex_sffi_spec.spl replaced the skipped placeholder with 28 real scenarios (compile valid/invalid/checked, match checked tri-state incl invalid-handle Err, find/find_all, captures + captures_len, replace first/all/no-match, split, quick fns, aliases, common-pattern compilers, validators email/url/ipv4 with pinned oracles e.g. 256.1.1.1 to true, complex patterns, legacy-path leg through app.io.regex_ffi - all WITHOUT unsafe blocks). Verification: regex_sffi_spec 28/28 PASS, legacy_ffi_facades 3/3, regex_legacy_facade_behavior 3/3 (its now-unnecessary unsafe blocks harmless - probed no warning), capability_truth 11/11, plugin/manifest 5/5, wrapper_gen/plugin_manifest 2/2; visibility warnings on the same compile dropped 112 to 83 (regex-name warnings eliminated); no new warning kinds; no any; regex_captures_len -> i64 preserved. Residuals: the owner module intentionally retains @unsafe ABI wrappers (same as compress/ftp); the shared sffi_common is_valid_handle visibility warning remains (pre-existing, cross-module). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/app/io/regex_sffi_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/app/io/legacy_ffi_facades_spec.spl"

